---
term: Nested corporation
section: structure
order: 10
definition: A corporation that sits inside a larger corporation and can contain smaller corporations of its own.
seeAlso:
  - constituent-corporation
  - parent-corporation
---
Each level has its own charter and its own common interest. One possible progression runs from the individual to a small association, a local corporation, a regional corporation, a national corporation, and higher-order corporations. Because corporations can have several parents, the full structure is a [[charter graph]], not a single ladder.

Elinor Ostrom found the same structure in long-lasting commons institutions and listed it as her eighth design principle, *nested enterprises*.
